# The build context is the repo root (docker-compose.yml sets context: .) because
# the Dockerfile COPYs every workspace manifest. Without this file that context is
# 278 MB, 264 MB of it host node_modules — which "COPY . ." then layers on top of
# the Alpine npm ci, replacing musl binaries like better_sqlite3.node with the
# glibc ones built for the host.
#
# ponytail: mirrors .gitignore. Anything git ignores here is a secret, a database,
# or a build output the builder stage regenerates from source. Note Docker does not
# use gitignore semantics — a bare "node_modules" would match only the root one, so
# every rule needs the **/ prefix.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.svelte-kit
**/coverage
**/.turbo

# Secrets and live data. Neither reaches the production stage today (it never runs
# "COPY . ."), but they have no business in the builder layers or the build cache.
# .env.example is deliberately kept — it is documentation.
**/.env
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

**/.git
**/.github
**/.DS_Store
media
data
